    <body>
        <segment id="1" parent="9" relname="background">I agree with you totally.</segment>
        <segment id="2" parent="9" relname="span">My experience with web development have shown me what happens when sites are designed for a particular audience.</segment>
        <segment id="3" parent="2" relname="elaboration">for example, when sites are designed for those that use Internet Explorer browsers only, or sites that are designed for those who have cookies enabled on their machines.</segment>
        <segment id="4" parent="7" relname="span">Universality is very important when it comes to the web.</segment>
        <segment id="5" parent="7" relname="evidence">good design principles and guidelines can help towards standardizations that can help to achive cross-platform, universally accesssible websites.</segment>
        <group id="6" type="span"/>
